# Transition state for K + HOO- -> KP (COMPUTATIONAL.md C8), catalyst = the
# full 130-atom active-site-ketone macrocycle (../../species/K, once that's
# populated), HOO- from the pre-reaction complex in ../rc/.
#
# Geometry: job.009.xyz from ../scan's relaxed xtb-level angle scan
# (A 130 128 129, 112 -> 75 deg, 10 steps) -- the scan's own energy maximum,
# E = -278.526207878820 (xtb/ALPB(water)), used as the TS guess. See
# ../scan/job.inp for the scan and ../legacy_pre-reorg/README.md for why an
# older, unreconstructable IRC/TS attempt in this folder was set aside rather
# than reused.
#
# Method: QM/XTB, r2SCAN-3c on the reactive QM region / GFN-xTB on the rest of
# the macrocycle, ALPB(water) -- the geometry/TS/Hessian tier established for
# this project 2026-09-09 (COMPUTATIONAL.md Conventions). Not the final
# energy: r2SCAN-3c systematically underestimates barrier heights relative to
# CCSD(T) (no exact exchange), which is why C8's own 4 kJ/mol-wide gate needs
# the DLPNO-CCSD(T) fragment correction run separately once this converges
# (see ../../energy_dlpno-ccsdt/, built on the OLD guess geometry -- rerun it
# on this TS's own job.QMRegion.xyz once optimised).
#
# QM region: the 8 atoms the original catHO2(-)+BnOH/TS/job.inp declared
# before this reorg, PLUS atom 132. The 8-atom list turned out to have never
# actually been run -- it aborts at multiscale setup, because atom 146's only
# boundary partner (132) is a hydrogen and ORCA refuses to cut there ("Cannot
# cut boundaries with hydrogen atoms. Please include atom 132 in the QM
# region." -- its own suggested fix, taken verbatim; 132 is monovalent so this
# adds no further boundary). ORCA also warns atom 128 has two link atoms (120,
# 124) -- non-fatal, left as is. Charge -1, singlet: matches the whole system
# (net charge sits entirely on HOO-'s deprotonated oxygen, inside the QM
# region).
#
# Calc_Hess true: fresh analytic/numeric Hessian at this level rather than
# reading the old job.xtbhess.xyz in ../legacy_pre-reorg/ -- that Hessian's
# own geometry doesn't match this one (see the README there), so it would be
# an inconsistent starting curvature, not a time-saver.
#
# nprocs 8 / maxcore 4000: same homelab-benchmarked settings as the fragment
# jobs (COMPUTATIONAL.md Conventions, 2026-09-09) -- this system is much
# bigger (147 atoms total) but the QM/XTB partition keeps the expensive
# (r2SCAN-3c) part small, so the same core count should still be
# communication-bound rather than compute-bound; revisit if wall time says
# otherwise.

! QM/XTB r2SCAN-3c ALPB(Water) OptTS Freq TightSCF

%QMMM
QMATOMS
	{146 130 128 131 137 139 136 133 132}
END
Charge_total -1
Mult_total 1
END

%geom
Calc_Hess true
END

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile -1 1 job.xyz
